[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678391972","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103248#issuecomment-2678391972","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103248","id":2678391972,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fpQSk","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T13:17:10Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T13:17:10Z","body":"If this is merged, I highly recommend calling it `script_will_change` because `script_changing` does not imply whether the signal is notified before or after the change.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678391972/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":1,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":1,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678532786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103248#issuecomment-2678532786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103248","id":2678532786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fpyqy","user":{"login":"TML233","id":19572238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NTcyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19572238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233","html_url":"https://github.com/TML233","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T14:12:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T14:41:53Z","body":"> If this is merged, I highly recommend calling it `script_will_change` because `script_changing` does not imply whether the signal is notified before or after the change.\r\n\r\n`doing` means before and `done` means after.\r\nAlso, there is no reference to `xxx_will_do` naming scheme but multiple references to `xxx_doing` naming scheme. For example: \r\n* `EditorFileSystem.resources_reimporting`(Emitted before a resource is reimported)\r\n* `Node.tree_exiting`(Emitted when the node is just about to exit the tree)\r\n* ...\r\n\r\nHere are the search results of two naming schemes. Some results in `xxx_doing` unrelated to \"signal emitted before the thing\" is removed. But not a single result is found for `xxx_will_do`.\r\n\r\n| xxx_doing | xxx_will_do |\r\n|------------|-------------|\r\n|![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/41cc510b-eab2-43cf-90b6-a76cdff58c82)|![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/21ceed71-efb9-43ab-b4b5-f6fdfa7a897b)|","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678532786/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678693542","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103248#issuecomment-2678693542","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103248","id":2678693542,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fqZ6m","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T14:52:20Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T14:52:35Z","body":"> Also, there is no reference to xxx_will_do naming scheme but multiple references to xxx_doing naming scheme. \r\n\r\nThanks for doing research on that. This is a legitimate argument.\r\nIf I would have been here back then, I would have asked people to rename these other signals, too. Changing the name for them is unfortunately out of question now.\r\nI would still recommend to make chronology explicit for new signals being introduced —  I'm not married to `will_x`, but I would definitely prefer a name that makes it clear which comes first.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678693542/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678694705","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103248#issuecomment-2678694705","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103248","id":2678694705,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fqaMx","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T14:52:40Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T14:52:40Z","body":"What about `before_script_change`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2678694705/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2680733293","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103248#issuecomment-2680733293","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103248","id":2680733293,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fyL5t","user":{"login":"TML233","id":19572238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NTcyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19572238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233","html_url":"https://github.com/TML233","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-25T06:13:55Z","updated_at":"2025-02-25T06:14:55Z","body":"> What about `before_script_change`?\n\nIt doesn't seem to look as good and paired as `script_changing` + `script_changed`. Further more, `doing` can be found in multiple previous signal names, and this naming scheme has also been adopted in various other languages and frameworks, such as Javascript and WPF.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2680733293/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689824044","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103248#issuecomment-2689824044","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103248","id":2689824044,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gU3Us","user":{"login":"TML233","id":19572238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NTcyMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19572238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233","html_url":"https://github.com/TML233","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TML233/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-28T06:17:42Z","updated_at":"2025-02-28T06:19:12Z","body":"> IMHO the name is fine. Maybe not perfect, but the doc and behavior should make it pretty clear what it provides. Not to bikeshed too much but another option with precedence in the codebase could be like `script_pre_changed`.\n> \n> \n> \n> Would it be at all useful to pass the new script as a signal parameter? Everything I can think of could be accomplished without such a parameter but maybe there's some niche case made possible by being able to check the incoming script's properties.\n\nThank you for your comment on the docs!\n\nMy purpose of this signal is to let the old script cleans up the changes it does, revert the state back to the clean one. And this clean state already suits for any incoming new script.\nIf a script only works when something else prepares the environment for it just before it attaches, I'd think that the script is not well designed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2689824044/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]